CORE gcc-only gcc16 libstdcxx16
main.cpp
--cpp17 --unwind 6 --no-unwinding-assertions
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ string from a literal: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
dropped the body
--
Was KNOWNBUG with the headers of libstdc++ 16 (gcc 16) only: basic_string's
four same-named `_M_construct' members got each other's out-of-line bodies
(matched by base name), `_M_local_buf[__len++] = *__beg' in an anonymous union
was "not an lvalue", and a definition renaming a parameter (`__str') left the
body with an unknown symbol.  Fixed in round 161
(cpp11_out_of_line_member_template_overloads,
cpp11_anonymous_union_array_member_lvalue).  Runs where the host gcc is >= 16
(tag libstdcxx16).  Round 162: no system-header body is dropped any more
(the `basic_string(const _CharT *, const _Alloc &)' constructors of the other
character types converted once out-of-line member templates of a class were
matched by signature and speculative constructor-template instances stopped
being converted).
